{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "2e781d86-2a24-4ee9-95fd-26a051e0aeff"/*CustomGeometryAttribute*/,
  "Description": "Writes a named attribute on the points, vertices, primitives or parts of a geometry from a C# snippet that runs for every element.\n\nThe snippet can read other attributes as @Name, so it covers constants (`return 1;`), copies (`return @Other;`) and any formula of them. The attribute flows with the geometry, so downstream ops can use it: [ExtrudeCurves] can scale its depth by a part attribute, [ColorGeometry] can map it to colors, and [TransformGeometry] can use a float as selection. A selection blends the new value over the old one, so only the selected elements change. To sample a field, use [AttributeFromField].\n\nAKA: attribute create, attribute wrangle, set attribute, SetGeometryAttribute\n\nTips\n- A snippet on the Parts of [StringToCurves] gives every letter its own value, e.g. `return 0.5f + 0.5f * Sin(i * 0.8f + A);`; animate A to move it.\n- `return @Normal.Y * A;` on Vertices reads the normals of a mesh.",
  "InputUis": [
    {
      "InputId": "19ea3de4-7a2a-4368-9360-a50123280689"/*Selection*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 540.0
      },
      "Description": "Name of a float selection whose weight blends the new value over the old one. Empty uses the Selection from an upstream [SelectGeometry] if there is one, and otherwise sets every element. All ignores any selection.",
      "Usage": "CustomDropdown"
    },
    {
      "InputId": "5fdbbd34-2144-4ba0-bea1-2866726ca09b"/*A*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 360.0
      },
      "Description": "Free parameter for the Custom snippet, e.g. to animate it."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "6b66dbbd-7d8d-4e98-845c-d472bb1cf296"/*Domain*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 45.0
      },
      "Description": "Which elements get the attribute: points, vertices, primitives (polygons and curves) or parts."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "837cd3ee-d92e-46c3-8d42-69f438c81e50"/*Code*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 315.0
      },
      "GroupTitle": "Custom",
      "Description": "Body of a C# method that returns the attribute's type (a float for Float and Int). In scope: index i, element count, position p (a primitive's center, a part's pivot) and the parameters A and B. System.MathF is imported, e.g. `return 0.5f + 0.5f * Sin(i * 0.8f + A);`. Attributes of the input geometry are read as @Name, e.g. `@Normal.Y` or `@Selection` after an upstream [SelectGeometry]; the Table tab of the input lists them. Attributes on points are converted to the chosen domain; @P is the position.",
      "Usage": "Code",
      "CodeLanguage": "CSharp"
    },
    {
      "InputId": "945f7c9d-fef3-40fa-bd00-b612dc3a7979"/*Name*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 90.0
      },
      "Description": "Name of the attribute to write, e.g. Depth for the depth of each part of an extrusion, or Color.",
      "Usage": "CustomDropdown"
    },
    {
      "InputId": "a9170934-849e-4dcf-9202-89385090e6de"/*B*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 405.0
      },
      "Description": "Free parameter for the Custom snippet."
    },
    {
      "InputId": "e469fa5c-3838-4af1-9e48-7bcb0a687f33"/*Geometry*/,
      "Relevancy": "Required",
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 0.0
      }
    },
    {
      "InputId": "f1f1fde1-9f97-4618-a020-aa6c800b7466"/*Type*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 0.0,
        "Y": 135.0
      },
      "Description": "Value type of the attribute and of what the snippet returns: a float for Float and Int, otherwise the vector type."
    }
  ],
  "SymbolChildUis": [],
  "OutputUis": [
    {
      "OutputId": "e90cfe0e-c1e8-461e-b755-431b9929f017"/*Result*/,
      "Position": {
        "X": 300.0,
        "Y": 0.0
      }
    }
  ]
}